From f425b2c799cfc72d04c210b932af53e738979e19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 14:49:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arifi-sync: register the three lane-209 mechanisms this
 integration lands

The protected-win guard refused at the integration tip on 4bbebd619, correctly:
it carries a Measured-effect trailer and no manifest entry covered it. Ranks 4
and 5 carry no trailer, so `discover` never saw them, but they are exactly the
class of measured win the mandate exists to keep from being overwritten. All
three are registered together rather than filing only the one the gate named.

- vulkan-iq4xs-matvec-dedicated (1884a620a)
- vulkan-iq3s-matvec-tpb16-union-gate (aa9f0e2aa) - the GATE is the win
- vulkan-q6k-matvec-direct-scales (4bbebd619) - a KEPT NEUTRAL; no speed claim

Every field is hand-authored from the lane report and the commit messages; no
field is derived from a trailer and no field is invented. The rank-7 ROCmFP4
MMVQ mechanism is deliberately NOT registered here - its integration disposition
is still open pending the n=3/n=5 adversarial numerical gate.

The measured numbers in these entries were produced on engine-r5/engine-r4c,
which are not the integration-tip binary, and are labelled lane-binary facts.

Evidence: research/local-inference/lane-evidence/2026-09-02-lane-209/r8-integrate/
---
 tools/arifi-sync/protected-wins.json | 45 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 45 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tools/arifi-sync/protected-wins.json b/tools/arifi-sync/protected-wins.json
index ffc0013cf..4a646411e 100644
--- a/tools/arifi-sync/protected-wins.json
+++ b/tools/arifi-sync/protected-wins.json
@@ -377,6 +377,51 @@
       "measured_effect": "UNMEASURED ON THIS SEAT (no Metal silicon). THIRD-PARTY reference from tq3/master, quoted and not adopted as ours: M3 Pro 27B decode ~4 t/s, about 27x over CPU (02d51f048).",
       "valid_conditions": "Apple Metal devices running TQ3_4S. Carried capability, inert here, not broken.",
       "notes": "protected_paths are shared upstream Metal files, so an upstream Metal bump will refuse this entry until a comparison is recorded. Accepted deliberately: there is no Metal file that is wholly ours, and the alternative is a capability nobody on this estate can test disappearing without anyone noticing. The dispatch-hook placement is part of the win - the tip regression it restores is the failure mode to compare against."
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "vulkan-iq4xs-matvec-dedicated",
+      "status": "active",
+      "_registered": "2026-09-05, lane-206 integration (R8). Landed on the integration branch by merge of lane-209/kernels; registered at the same time so the mechanism is guarded before any upstream bump touches it.",
+      "mechanism": "IQ4_XS gets a dedicated K-quant-style mat-vec shader (16 threads per 256-superblock, each thread taking both nibble halves of 2 packed32 words = 16 MACs per row per superblock, sub-block scale decoded once per row per superblock) instead of the generic mul_mat_vec.comp, which re-decoded the scale per dequantize4() call and used only one nibble half of each fetched word. Routed by `tname == \"iq4_xs\"` in vulkan-shaders-gen.cpp; the MUL_MAT_ID vec path picks up the same shader.",
+      "commit": "1884a620a",
+      "protected_paths": ["ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/mul_mat_vec_iq4_xs.comp", "ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/vulkan-shaders-gen.cpp"],
+      "anchors": ["mul_mat_vec_iq4_xs.comp", "tname == \"iq4_xs\""],
+      "evidence": ["board/programs/local-inference/lanes/2026-09-02-lane-209-kernel-attacks-REPORT.md", "research/local-inference/lane-evidence/2026-09-02-lane-209/r5", "commit:1884a620a"],
+      "quality_gate": "test-backend-ops -o MUL_MAT and -o MUL_MAT_ID, 0 FAIL; F-141 content floor 0/8 on every slot with the baseline arm run first. A dequant mat-vec kernel fails silently, so a speed number alone is never the gate.",
+      "workload": "Radeon 780M gfx1103 Vulkan, llama-server serve A/B on U-IQ4XS and U-Q3KXL, DFlash2 Q4_K_M drafter at --spec-draft-n-max 2 (df2) and plain; palindrome 2 launches x 8 rounds per slot, cell-wise CI95. Op-level ladder: test-backend-ops perf m=17408 k=5120 n=1,2,3,4,5,8.",
+      "measured_effect": "LANE-BINARY MEASUREMENT (engine-before -> engine-r5, epochs E1/E2, matched 2x16 GB RAM): U-IQ4XS df2 +0.617 t/s [+0.255, +0.978], 8/8 cells positive; U-Q3KXL df2 +0.293 [+0.060, +0.527]; U-Q3KXL plain +0.742 [+0.208, +1.276]. Op ladder 98-105% of q4_K at n=1..4. U-IQ4XS plain +9.5% median with a CI straddling zero on both takes.",
+      "valid_conditions": "Radeon 780M gfx1103 under Vulkan; models carrying a material IQ4_XS share (U-IQ4XS 49.7%, U-Q3KXL 36.6%, U-Q4KM 28.7% by bytes). No remote carries an IQ4_XS mat-vec shader, so there is no upstream arm to compare against - an incoming change that adds one is a named collision, not a free replacement.",
+      "notes": "Registered from the lane's banked verdict, not re-measured at registration time. The numbers above were produced on engine-r5, a different binary from the integration tip; a different tree produces a different binary, so they are lane-binary facts and must be labelled as such."
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "vulkan-iq3s-matvec-tpb16-union-gate",
+      "status": "active",
+      "_registered": "2026-09-05, lane-206 integration (R8), same reasoning as the IQ4_XS row above.",
+      "mechanism": "IQ3_S mat-vec runs 16 invocations per superblock (zuijdwijk 211abf6a9 body, via lane-166) at the UNION of the widths where it wins on this box: ARIFI_TPB16 = (NUM_COLS == 3) || (NUM_COLS > 4). NUM_COLS 3 is the DFlash2 n-max-2 verify width. Widths 1, 2 and 4 keep the upstream body bit for bit, because the no-sum[] form measured 7-9% slower at n=2 and about 20% slower at n=4 on the 780M - the `>= 2` gate (616b877b8) is superseded by this union gate for exactly that reason.",
+      "commit": "aa9f0e2aa",
+      "protected_paths": ["ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/mul_mat_vec_iq3_s.comp"],
+      "anchors": ["ARIFI_TPB16"],
+      "evidence": ["board/programs/local-inference/lanes/2026-09-02-lane-209-kernel-attacks-REPORT.md", "research/local-inference/lane-evidence/2026-09-02-lane-209/r4c", "commit:aa9f0e2aa"],
+      "quality_gate": "test-backend-ops -o MUL_MAT and -o MUL_MAT_ID, 0 FAIL; F-141 content floor 0/8 on every slot, baseline arm first.",
+      "workload": "Radeon 780M gfx1103 Vulkan, llama-server serve A/B on U-Q3KXL (iq3_s 26.6% by bytes) and U-IQ4XS (11.3%), df2 and plain, palindrome 2 launches x 8 rounds per slot. Op ladder test-backend-ops perf m=17408 k=5120 across n.",
+      "measured_effect": "LANE-BINARY MEASUREMENT (engine-r5 -> engine-r4c, E1/E2, matched 2x16 GB RAM): U-Q3KXL df2 +0.820 t/s [+0.622, +1.018], 8/8 positive (8.367 -> 9.268, +10.8%); U-IQ4XS df2 +0.198 [-0.033, +0.430] take 1 and +0.199 [-0.004, +0.403] take 2, agreeing to three decimals across a driver epoch; plain arms identical, as the control predicts. Kernel ladder: n=3 39.7 -> 53.8 GB/s = +35%, n=5 x1.472, n=8 x4.803, n=1/2/4 unchanged bit for bit.",
+      "valid_conditions": "Radeon 780M gfx1103 under Vulkan, models with a material IQ3_S share. The width GATE is itself the win: an incoming change that widens or narrows ARIFI_TPB16 must be compared at n=1..8 on this box before it replaces the union, because the 16-invocation body is measurably WORSE at n=2 and n=4 here.",
+      "notes": "Body taken from zuijdwijk 211abf6a9; the gate is ours and is the part that must not be overwritten. Registered from the lane verdict; the numbers are lane-binary facts, not integration-tip measurements."
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "vulkan-q6k-matvec-direct-scales",
+      "status": "active",
+      "_registered": "2026-09-05, lane-206 integration (R8). Registered as a KEPT NEUTRAL: no speed win is claimed here and none may be quoted from this entry.",
+      "mechanism": "mul_mat_vec_q6_k.comp reads its 16 int8 superblock scales directly out of the block instead of staging them through a double-buffered LDS tile with a barrier() per row. The exchange moved no data between threads, so the direct read is bit-identical by construction, and measured so. Specialization constant 3 selects the path; GGML_VK_Q6K_DIRECT_SCALES=0 restores upstream's LDS path byte for byte in the same binary.",
+      "commit": "4bbebd619",
+      "protected_paths": ["ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/mul_mat_vec_q6_k.comp"],
+      "anchors": ["GGML_VK_Q6K_DIRECT_SCALES"],
+      "evidence": ["research/local-inference/lane-evidence/2026-09-02-lane-209/rank3-r10/OPUS-5-R7-780M-KERNEL-ATTACK-REPORT.md", "commit:4bbebd619"],
+      "quality_gate": "test-backend-ops -o MUL_MAT 1394/1394, 0 FAIL, on BOTH arms; plus byte-identical llama-server output between the arms (1 distinct sha256 per prompt across all arm-launches). Bit-identity is the gate this entry lives or dies on - it is the whole basis for keeping a change that buys no measured speed.",
+      "workload": "Radeon 780M gfx1103 Vulkan, Huihui-Qwen3.8-27B UD-Q4_K_XL + DFlash2 Q4_K_M drafter at --spec-draft-n-max 2; one binary, arms env-gated, 6 position-balanced interleaved launches per phase, Balanced power plan, 32+16 GB asymmetric RAM.",
+      "measured_effect": "NEUTRAL on gfx1103, and that is the whole claim. Op level: q6_k rows median ON/OFF 0.9796 against a control of 78 untouched op rows at 0.9990, p10-p90 [0.952, 1.053] - no q6_k row separates. Serve level TIED on all six prefill/decode cells at three prompt lengths. Output byte-identical, 1 sha256 per prompt over 12 arm-launches. NO SPEED WIN IS CLAIMED.",
+      "valid_conditions": "Kept because it is strictly less work for a bit-identical result - one fewer workgroup barrier per row per superblock, and no shared-memory tile - on an engine that ships to other people's hardware, where LDS pressure and barrier cost are not what they are on a 780M. Protected as a NEUTRAL: an incoming upstream change that reverts it is not a regression to fight on speed grounds here, but it must be compared rather than silently taken, because the mechanism's value is off-seat.",
+      "notes": "Also banks the falsification the next attempt needs: the per-row barrier was the leading mechanism for q6_k's reproducible ~35% mat-vec deficit on this box (41.0 GB/s against q5_k 63.8 and q4_k 72.5 at m=17408 n=3 k=5120). Removing it moves nothing. The deficit stands, unexplained."
     }
   ]
 }
